sk for the option below the knee, the lean and the top option; tasks state no case counts, so these figures are descriptive."}]}, {"id": "failures", "weight": "detail", "text": "The lean's kept failures are planning errors: a collapsed hop, an off-by-one date window, and a guess where it should have asked.", "evidence": [{"block": "examples", "query": {"source": "examples", "aspect": "", "measures": [], "arms": ["brisk-s.low.r1"], "strata": [], "limit": 0, "transform": "none", "small_multiples_by": "none"}, "caption": "Every failure the snapshot keeps for the lean, one per task where kept; the run's total failures are not counted, so these show kinds, not shares."}]}], "explore": [{"control": "Price of a point of pass rate a month", "binds": "Which frontier option is the best buy", "outcome": "Below {price.nano-xs.high.r1.brisk-s.low.r1.pass_rate.monthly_per_point} a cheaper option wins; up to {price.brisk-s.low.r1.brisk-s.high.r1.pass_rate.monthly_per_point} the lean holds; up to {price.brisk-s.high.r1.atlas-m.high.r1.pass_rate.monthly_per_point} {arm:brisk-s.high.r1} does; above that, {arm:atlas-m.high.r1}. Point prices, no interval."}, {"control": "A pass-rate floor, read on point estimates", "binds": "The cheapest option that clears it", "outcome": "The lean is cheapest for floors above {measure.pass_rate.brisk-s.low.r0.mean} up to {measure.pass_rate.brisk-s.low.r1.mean}; {arm:brisk-s.high.r1} up to {measure.pass_rate.brisk-s.high.r1.mean}; above that only {arm:atlas-m.high.r1} clears, up to {measure.pass_rate.atlas-m.high.r1.mean}."}, {"control": "A p95 latency budget", "binds": "Which options stay in", "outcome": "A budget under {measure.latency_ms.brisk-s.low.r1.p95} rules the lean out; every Atlas-M option reads at or above {measure.latency_ms.atlas-m.off.r0.p95}."}], "omitted": [{"what": "The options off the frontier", "why": "Each costs more than another option that passes at least as many tasks; they are in the full tables."}, {"what": "The other retry ef